diagnosis_text:
OSPF across the core is healthy and stable; there is no flapping router or backbone link to restart. Evidence:
- All core adjacencies are Full and steady. On router_core_1, router_core_2, and router_core_3, “show ip ospf neighbor detail” shows Full/DR or Full/Backup with “Most recent state change ~53–99s ago” and “6 state changes.” The “6 state changes” correspond to the normal OSPF state-machine progression (Down→Init→2-Way→ExStart→Exchange→Loading→Full) at startup, not repeated flaps.
- FRR logs on all three cores contain only initial configuration reads and one-time DD negotiation, with no repeated neighbor down/up messages.
